,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{3}^{4}(2 t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[t^{2}\\right]_{3}^{4} \\\\ &=\\left(16\\right)-\\left(9\\right) \\\\ &=7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44276bca-91ea-547c-8bcd-8305137a0d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712777} {:answer/id #uuid "6859962e-a77d-526e-bb1b-2235992b0afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712782} {:answer/id #uuid "c202b4e0-bf19-5ba9-b6ec-4f8d9f69e16a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712792} {:answer/id #uuid "d266018d-1a20-5f96-9066-875a4b0fb25a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1568}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712795} {:answer/id #uuid "da802c0e-aee3-5b9d-a0f1-ad9311dffbf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6859962e-a77d-526e-bb1b-2235992b0afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712782} :answer-field/id #uuid "523e1641-f219-5915-93a8-537d33136284" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "daecc408-83e3-5a98-ae1e-7c72e0ef0eb3" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve with coordinate functions\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t)&=- 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} - 2 \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\\\ y(t)&=\\sqrt{3} t^{2} - 2 \\\\ z(t)&=- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=3$ to $t=5$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the coordinates and simplify the speed. Since $t\\ge 0$ on this interval, $|t|=t$. Use $\\sin^2(\\theta)+\\cos^2(\\theta)=1$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=-2\\left(-\\sin t+(\\sin t+t\\cos t)\\right) \\\\ &=- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ y'(t)&=2\\sqrt{3} t \\\\ z'(t)&=2\\left(\\cos t-(\\cos t-t\\sin t)\\right) \\\\ &=2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=\\left(- 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &\\quad+\\left(2\\sqrt{3} t\\right)^2+\\left(2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)^2 \\\\ &=16 t^{2} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{16 t^{2}} \\\\ &=4|t| \\\\ &=4 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{3}^{5}\\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\int_{3}^{5}(4 t)\\,\\mathrm dt \\\\ &=\\left[2 t^{2}\\right]_{3}^{5} \\\\ &=\\left(50\\right)-\\left(18\\right) \\\\ &=32\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16e16a67-b560-5527-aff6-5597b03a61d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\sqrt{2} e + 3 \\sqrt{2} e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712801} {:answer/id #uuid "3897d0aa-7f40-5b95-810d-ffd199581519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 \\sqrt{2} e + 6 \\sqrt{2} e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712807} {:answer/id #uuid "7beeb000-ec17-5983-85ba-2249e60ca9e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{2} e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712820} {:answer/id #uuid "88b50089-1790-56f9-bf62-4606c613425f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{2} e + 3 \\sqrt{2} e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712822} {:answer/id #uuid "df3c65d4-74d0-5177-ac54-440b7995703e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 9 e^{2} + 9 e^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16e16a67-b560-5527-aff6-5597b03a61d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 \\sqrt{2} e + 3 \\sqrt{2} e^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712801} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3702be5-346e-5608-8b8f-c3ec4bf5d5b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3006f742-be90-5a22-8b33-d539bb1c0159" :question/problem "![The specified curve segment is blue; its continuation is red. Diagram is schematic.](images/06/06b1a26e87ee3098d7fee1fda264fb30f67bfe45187b0d2ed94b0e0a79c2877a.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\begin{pmatrix}3 e^{t} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\ - 3 e^{t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=1$ to $t=2$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate both components and simplify the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=3 \\left(- \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{t} \\\\ y'(t)&=- 3 \\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{t} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=x'(t)^2+y'(t)^2 \\\\ &=9 e^{2 t}\\left(1\\cos(t)^2+1\\sin(t)^2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad-18 e^{2 t}\\cos(t)\\sin(t) \\\\ &\\quad+9 e^{2 t}\\left(1\\sin(t)^2+1\\cos(t)^2\\right) \\\\ &\\quad+18 e^{2 t}\\cos(t)\\sin(t) \\\\ &=18 e^{2 t}\\left(\\cos(t)^2+\\sin(t)^2\\right) \\\\ &=18 e^{2 t} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=3 \\sqrt{2} e^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe mixed terms cancel. Use the Pythagorean identity, then take the nonnegative square root; the exponential factor is positive.\n\nIntegrate the speed over the parameter interval:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{1}^{2}3 \\sqrt{2} e^{t}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[3 \\sqrt{2} e^{t}\\right]_{1}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left(3 \\sqrt{2} e^{2}\\right)-\\left(3 \\sqrt{2} e\\right) \\\\ &=- 3 \\sqrt{2} e + 3 \\sqrt{2} e^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51cae9e6-d965-5f2b-a142-4e8b6bf5c0c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{44 - 12 \\sqrt{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712810} {:answer/id #uuid "5b36352f-51eb-5122-8374-2bef34804216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712812} {:answer/id #uuid "69e6039f-e4db-5d9e-b70b-960ac945187d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712817} {:answer/id #uuid "795e2e08-15f7-5328-8b6e-6e3de024ccaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712818} {:answer/id #uuid "da1586bb-a540-5569-b1d5-856e35648a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da1586bb-a540-5569-b1d5-856e35648a58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712829} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f8cf9b7-0137-556c-834d-f8540e5fe082" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "638ad279-3637-57f1-b05a-87cb7af7f03e" :question/problem "![The specified curve segment is blue; its continuation is red.](images/33/33881da11a22dfce762540152077ec781246851e035a091b8ec9d7f3f03702b0.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\begin{pmatrix}2 - 3 t \\\\ - \\left(t^{2} + 2\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}} - 1\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=1$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate both components and simplify the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=-3 \\\\ y'(t)&=- 3 t \\sqrt{t^{2} + 2} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=x'(t)^2+y'(t)^2 \\\\ &=9 t^{4} + 18 t^{2} + 9 \\\\ &=\\left(3 t^{2} + 3\\right)^2 \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=3 t^{2} + 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the nonnegative square root. Here $t^2+1>0$.\n\nIntegrate the speed over the parameter interval:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{1}3 t^{2} + 3\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[t^{3} + 3 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\ &=\\left(4\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\ &=4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d08a79f-d541-5510-808a-8cbd8866d90e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712802} {:answer/id #uuid "2318e64a-a177-5107-9ea9-1245f551e92a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712803} {:answer/id #uuid "61778bf3-b516-5a2f-b493-3748e3236c56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712814} {:answer/id #uuid "6690db21-c766-5063-bb44-ac779e091425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712816} {:answer/id #uuid "79ea62e2-ee60-56be-8543-fc7101520b9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3057}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61778bf3-b516-5a2f-b493-3748e3236c56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712814} :answer-field/id #uuid "23c43027-8f10-58a8-8d45-38800e492030" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7e370f80-1db6-5d59-a354-69c7227562ef" :question/problem "![The specified curve segment is blue; its continuation is red. Diagram is schematic.](images/1d/1d9cdd9736c6157b606bcaf05c74dbdb2f29403c8d89bb2220e4c025caff266a.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\begin{pmatrix}6 t \\\\ - t^{3} - \\frac{3}{t}\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=1$ to $t=2$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate both components and simplify the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=6 \\\\ y'(t)&=- 3 t^{2} + \\frac{3}{t^{2}} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=x'(t)^2+y'(t)^2 \\\\ &=9 t^{4} + 18 + \\frac{9}{t^{4}} \\\\ &=\\left(3 t^{2} + \\frac{3}{t^{2}}\\right)^2 \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=3 t^{2} + \\frac{3}{t^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the nonnegative square root.\n\nIntegrate the speed over the parameter interval:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{1}^{2}3 t^{2} + \\frac{3}{t^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[t^{3} - \\frac{3}{t}\\right]_{1}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left(\\frac{13}{2}\\right)-\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712825 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ff4739b-b842-5223-ad2c-c02e1719c66f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712809} {:answer/id #uuid "573a97a0-03e3-5785-9d70-f1935f031d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{\\left(4 \\right)} - 4 \\cos{\\left(4 \\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712811} {:answer/id #uuid "a36676b6-a0f4-5302-9518-c0943757502d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712824} {:answer/id #uuid "b98ab43c-1f34-562d-9d21-26abbb570b6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{128}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712827} {:answer/id #uuid "ecb5f357-edf2-5278-ad29-c63e48caac82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecb5f357-edf2-5278-ad29-c63e48caac82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712831} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e98b98c-e3e1-58ca-9002-bf495c657845" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4d30682-f545-51ab-aa22-814873a55e49" :question/problem "![The specified curve segment is blue; its continuation is red.](images/07/071854a714bbde918f270519fe93085c7924439841c8c4e225316a59fe827c10.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\begin{pmatrix}- 2 t \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} - \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} + 2 \\\\ 2 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} - \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=0$ to $t=2$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate both components and simplify the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=- 4 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ y'(t)&=- 4 t \\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=x'(t)^2+y'(t)^2 \\\\ &=16 t^{2}(\\cos^2(2 t)+\\sin^2(2 t)) \\\\ &=16 t^{2} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=4|t| \\\\ &=4 t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product-rule terms cancel. Use the Pythagorean identity and $|t|=t$ on the stated interval.\n\nIntegrate the speed over the parameter interval:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{0}^{2}4 t\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[2 t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left(8\\right)-\\left(0\\right) \\\\ &=8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186712832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "166d5a2b-692d-5ba0-836a-6cd318d49e8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6 + 18 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712800} {:answer/id #uuid "2d8f0a3e-2fc7-5aad-9b01-5a18142f59f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108 - 36 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712805} {:answer/id #uuid "3b5ff8d0-072d-5c2d-8b0c-9291645c900e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48 - 12 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712808} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef14e7f-1463-568c-ac80-6ce7f5f4ec35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24 - 6 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712823} {:answer/id #uuid "fe01dd9b-db07-5779-a4f8-2a3ba3e7307b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96 - 24 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b5ff8d0-072d-5c2d-8b0c-9291645c900e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48 - 12 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712808} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa18dbe4-aedc-5922-856c-5a524f14575d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186712826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f47560f0-def8-5e98-bc28-de61844fea9c" :question/problem "![The specified curve segment is blue; its continuation is red.](images/96/96ffae4f794c38cd062149f5f0dea313b605e3a0e3961eaa9f09c16785d7c2a4.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\begin{pmatrix}6 t^{3} - 21 \\\\ - 9 t^{2} - 30\\end{pmatrix}\n$$\n\nfrom $t=- \\sqrt{3}$ to $t=-1$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate both components and simplify the speed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(t)&=18 t^{2} \\\\ y'(t)&=- 18 t \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|^2&=x'(t)^2+y'(t)^2 \\\\ &=324 t^{2}(t^2+1) \\\\ \\|\\mathbf r'(t)\\|&=18|t|\\sqrt{t^2+1} \\\\ &=- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSpeed is nonnegative; the factor $|t|$ comes from $\\sqrt{t^2}$. Here $|t|=-t$ on the entire interval.\n\nUse $u=t^2+1$, so $\\mathrm{d}u=2t\\,\\mathrm{d}t$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L&=\\int_{- \\sqrt{3}}^{-1}- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &=-9\\int_{4}^{2}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ &=\\left[- 6 u^{\\frac{3}{2}}\\right]_{4}^{2} \\\\ &=\\left(- 12 \\sqrt{2}\\right)-\\left(-48\\right) \\\\ &=48 - 12 \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716758 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2122170-3b96-5773-a6cc-e0f9cf3cceab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2122170-3b96-5773-a6cc-e0f9cf3cceab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716772} :answer-field/id #uuid "c94474ec-632b-55fb-a660-6f3d8c57ba0b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b8e08e5-4df6-523c-8c4e-e6486d55934d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b8e08e5-4df6-523c-8c4e-e6486d55934d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716768} :answer-field/id #uuid "f76fecec-0a30-556c-8831-6cb7492bd6c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "14b9cc54-aa02-5d9a-a941-ee128cea9e89" :question/problem "![Circle centered at O(0,0), passing through the top point A(0,2), with an arrow showing clockwise motion.](images/5f/5fec78eab6df87be10bae2cea167929b6bb0194a00b8db6083b8ca44d996111e.png)\n\nThe circle shown is centered at $O(0,0)$ and passes through $A(0,2)$. Construct a set of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$, that traverse this circle once clockwise, starting at $A$ when $\\theta=0$. Use one sine or cosine term with argument $\\theta$ in each equation.\n\n$x=$ {{field-1}}, $y=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The distance from $O(0,0)$ to $A(0,2)$ is $2$, so the radius is $2$.\n\nTo start at $(0,2)$ when $\\theta=0$, use sine for the $x$-coordinate and cosine for the $y$-coordinate:\n\n$$\nx=2\\sin\\theta,\\qquad y=2\\cos\\theta,\\qquad \\theta\\in[0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nFor a small positive $\\theta$, $x$ becomes positive and $y$ decreases from $2$, so the point moves right from the top, in the clockwise direction. The quarter-turn positions are\n\n$$\n(0,2)\\ \\longrightarrow\\ (2,0)\\ \\longrightarrow\\ (0,-2)\\ \\longrightarrow\\ (-2,0).\n$$\n\nAlso, $x^2+y^2=4(\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta)=4$, so the point stays on the required circle. The interval $[0,2\\pi)$ covers one full turn without repeating the starting point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ac987dc-2638-5d16-8f5c-1ae0a4a302b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ac987dc-2638-5d16-8f5c-1ae0a4a302b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716762} :answer-field/id #uuid "18643e21-3515-56d4-83e1-92a1501d73bc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716759} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66ae5de4-23f9-5bbf-8f98-41ae8087e319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66ae5de4-23f9-5bbf-8f98-41ae8087e319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716765} :answer-field/id #uuid "8acfbd8a-ac25-5845-a336-9526a226d3be" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "611c3217-cd7e-55c9-baf0-9ad79907362b" :question/problem "![Circle centered at the origin, with radius 2, starting at A(2,0) and directed counterclockwise.](images/15/156d160267551e9dbf4db42b14b1e0dbb46ab658a836a760cf31a42eb89662d3.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $2$ centered at the origin, as shown above. Construct a set of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$, that traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at $A(2,0)$ when $\\theta=0$. Use one sine or cosine term with argument $\\theta$ in each equation.\n\n$x=$ {{field-1}}, $y=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The standard parametrization of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the origin is\n\n$$\nx=r\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=r\\sin\\theta,\\qquad \\theta\\in[0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nIt starts at $(r,0)$ and moves counterclockwise. With $r=2$, the required equations are\n\n$$\nx=2\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=2\\sin\\theta,\\qquad \\theta\\in[0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nAt $\\theta=0$, the point is $(2,0)$. At $\\theta=\\pi/2$, it is $(0,2)$, confirming counterclockwise motion. As $\\theta$ increases through one full period, the circle is traversed once."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716773 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a88fd24-f438-5bf5-bc55-31ef242cd75e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=2\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716760} {:answer/id #uuid "1aa899fa-5b83-568a-a222-06f0aaec77f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=4\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716761} {:answer/id #uuid "63b199c1-1e03-581f-bb14-d0ff48c3a14e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\sqrt{2}\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716764} {:answer/id #uuid "873ab139-7e97-5511-a2ba-d988123f3882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716766} {:answer/id #uuid "deaade05-3764-5a0e-ac40-25f5ad71ff3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=4\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a88fd24-f438-5bf5-bc55-31ef242cd75e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=2\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716760} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0743ef1-b337-5874-888c-4a7d867929f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef5c811d-79f8-5cb2-b97d-6caee9d23c73" :question/problem "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$, generate a circle of radius $2$ centered at the origin?" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=r\\sin\\theta,\\qquad \\theta\\in[0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $r=2$ gives\n\n$$\nx=2\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=2\\sin\\theta,\\qquad \\theta\\in[0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nBoth coordinates have amplitude $2$, so the radius is $2$. Unequal amplitudes would produce an ellipse, and equal amplitudes of a different size would give the wrong radius."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716779 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2030d656-8c03-5463-9cd8-2d46a9080ca8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\cos\\theta-3,\\quad y=4\\sin\\theta+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716776} {:answer/id #uuid "503450b9-4517-57bd-b0ba-a2671244611d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\cos\\theta+3,\\quad y=2\\sin\\theta-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716777} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b917d7-0912-561d-88e0-9ecb08acfe8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\cos\\theta+4,\\quad y=2\\sin\\theta-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716782} {:answer/id #uuid "a5854045-5cb7-5df4-8e6b-29eafc24274f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\cos\\theta-3,\\quad y=4\\sin\\theta+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716783} {:answer/id #uuid "f9ba7c55-59d5-56f9-85aa-ff70a03fba73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\cos\\theta-3,\\quad y=2\\sin\\theta+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9ba7c55-59d5-56f9-85aa-ff70a03fba73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\cos\\theta-3,\\quad y=2\\sin\\theta+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716791} :answer-field/id #uuid "aae40024-d16a-5006-95cc-0f851ac6f7c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97ee639c-5f23-5d5f-b9a5-ba51385fbf15" :question/problem "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$, generates a circle of radius $2$ centered at $(-3,4)$?" :question/worked-solution "A circle of radius $r$ centered at $(a,b)$ has the parametrization\n\n$$\nx=a+r\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=b+r\\sin\\theta,\\qquad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$\n\nHere $r=2$, $a=-3$, and $b=4$, so\n\n$$\nx=2\\cos\\theta-3,\\qquad y=2\\sin\\theta+4.\n$$\n\nBoth trigonometric coefficients must have magnitude $2$; the constant terms give the center $(-3,4)$. Reversing the signs of those constants changes the center, interchanging them swaps its coordinates, and using $4$ as both coefficients gives radius $4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716781 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e30d5a39-202e-5fc2-99bc-3a079373574f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos\\theta-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e30d5a39-202e-5fc2-99bc-3a079373574f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos\\theta-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716787} :answer-field/id #uuid "03cddba4-d4e0-5784-a50f-de87c66401c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716775} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec72f124-69e7-5bcc-9cc1-05a7febdbe97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin\\theta+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec72f124-69e7-5bcc-9cc1-05a7febdbe97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin\\theta+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716789} :answer-field/id #uuid "9064514b-c2e9-514f-8b7e-ebc5f2ba7f75" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9a164e43-037a-5a2f-b9da-bd7a490e97e7" :question/problem "![Circle centered at C(-2,1), with P(1,5) on its circumference and A at its rightmost point.](images/41/41afde8ef1206982455ac09b33650bd0a842d2ac50b1001bab590470404c402e.png)\n\nA circle has center $C(-2,1)$ and passes through $P(1,5)$. The point $A$ is its rightmost point. Construct parametric equations for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$ that traverse the circle once counterclockwise, starting at $A$ when $\\theta=0$. Use $\\cos\\theta$ in the $x$-equation and $\\sin\\theta$ in the $y$-equation.\n\n$x=$ {{field-1}}, $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The radius is the distance from the center $C$ to the point $P$:\n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{(1-(-2))^2+(5-1)^2}=\\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=5.\n$$\n\nA circle of radius $r$ centered at $(a,b)$ has the parametrization\n\n$$\nx=a+r\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=b+r\\sin\\theta,\\qquad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$\n\nWith $r=5$ and $(a,b)=(-2,1)$, the required equations are\n\n$$\nx=5\\cos\\theta-2,\\qquad y=5\\sin\\theta+1.\n$$\n\nAt $\\theta=0$, the point is $(3,1)$, the rightmost point $A$. At $\\theta=\\pi/2$, it is $(-2,6)$, above the center; thus the motion is counterclockwise. The interval $[0,2\\pi)$ gives exactly one traversal. Using $25$ in place of $5$ would confuse the squared radius with the radius."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9e29966-aa39-541b-af23-95818177be95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\cos\\theta-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9e29966-aa39-541b-af23-95818177be95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\cos\\theta-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716788} :answer-field/id #uuid "99301dcd-b6b6-5195-8f51-58acf6cf2916" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bda2ae25-0708-5b30-aa99-b4cfabc42576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin\\theta+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bda2ae25-0708-5b30-aa99-b4cfabc42576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin\\theta+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716785} :answer-field/id #uuid "d578ff75-1837-5763-ac9e-ac029bc754a5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716786}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f4bbff12-9fcb-5e90-836d-b82dfe41f9ce" :question/problem "![Circle centered at C(-2,3) with radius 4 and rightmost point A(2,3).](images/78/78429ab38480bd45ed608be7977f3102cfad84b9a190a61322ab25235ad2d7a0.png)\n\nThe circle shown has radius $4$ and center $C(-2,3)$. Construct parametric equations for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$ that traverse it once counterclockwise, starting at $A(2,3)$ when $\\theta=0$. Use $\\cos\\theta$ in the $x$-equation and $\\sin\\theta$ in the $y$-equation.\n\n$x=$ {{field-1}}, $y=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "A circle of radius $r$ centered at $(a,b)$ has the parametrization\n\n$$\nx=a+r\\cos\\theta,\\qquad y=b+r\\sin\\theta,\\qquad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $r=4$ and $(a,b)=(-2,3)$:\n\n$$\nx=4\\cos\\theta-2,\\qquad y=4\\sin\\theta+3.\n$$\n\nAt $\\theta=0$, this gives $(x,y)=(2,3)=A$. As $\\theta$ increases toward $\\pi/2$, the point moves upward to $(-2,7)$, so the traversal is counterclockwise. The interval $[0,2\\pi)$ covers the circle exactly once."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40dff972-cde3-5866-92be-5c3596131f24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40dff972-cde3-5866-92be-5c3596131f24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716922} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b57c72a-c1f4-591c-af21-da38be57af1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5057a17b-088d-50a0-a720-77641d86187d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5057a17b-088d-50a0-a720-77641d86187d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716923} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d00bc4f-647a-5b92-95a7-29f64e7376af" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716921} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e205797f-1b8d-5635-a7e4-e559d3198f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e205797f-1b8d-5635-a7e4-e559d3198f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716931} :answer-field/id #uuid "9257c360-e325-5078-9a6d-5af734a3b119" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "222f4e68-30f9-5455-ad2f-034cd25cba63" :question/problem "The Cartesian equation of the circle defined by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3}{2}\\cos\\theta-2,\\quad y=\\frac{3}{2}\\sin\\theta+1,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$(x+$ {{field-1}} $)^2+(y-$ {{field-2}} $)^2=$ {{field-3}}.\n\nFill in the three missing values." :question/worked-solution "First undo the translations, then isolate the trigonometric functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx+2&=\\frac{3}{2}\\cos\\theta &\\quad \\frac{2}{3}(x+2)&=\\cos\\theta\\\\\ny-1&=\\frac{3}{2}\\sin\\theta &\\quad \\frac{2}{3}(y-1)&=\\sin\\theta.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquare each equation and add. Using the Pythagorean identity gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{4}{9}(x+2)^2+\\frac{4}{9}(y-1)^2&=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta\\\\\n\\frac{4}{9}\\bigl((x+2)^2+(y-1)^2\\bigr)&=1\\\\\n(x+2)^2+(y-1)^2&=\\frac{9}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe three missing values are $2$, $1$, and $\\frac{9}{4}$, in that order. The center is $(-2,1)$ and the radius is $\\frac{3}{2}$. The signs already printed in the answer agree with subtracting the center coordinates. The full parameter interval traces the entire circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb54073-1769-5b14-a893-7aabe1fda6f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716915} {:answer/id #uuid "1a770563-0ef8-570e-acc9-49f52d074863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2-y^2=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716917} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4bf2b5-c749-580a-87d5-a657c62e5099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2-y^2=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716930} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f87172-ecff-5cf0-a02b-c37c635a7f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716932} {:answer/id #uuid "e4cff477-7af7-5e28-b596-25ae87327621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fb54073-1769-5b14-a893-7aabe1fda6f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716915} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa332b10-9b94-5744-ba77-2e5351b3e9f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71c30e19-732e-5a08-95ed-b00720f5774b" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=2\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=2\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$\n\nDividing each equation by $2$ and squaring gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{4}=\\cos^2\\theta,\\qquad \\frac{y^2}{4}=\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nUse $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$ to eliminate $\\theta$. Choose the Cartesian equation." :question/worked-solution "Add the two supplied equations and use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^2}{4}+\\frac{y^2}{4}&=\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta\\\\\n\\frac{x^2+y^2}{4}&=1\\\\\nx^2+y^2&=4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is $x^2+y^2=4$. The radius is $2$, so its square is $4$, not $2$ or $16$. The squared terms are added, not subtracted. The full parameter interval traces the entire circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716934 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0786e72d-fdb6-5b51-a5bb-f94092553887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716914} {:answer/id #uuid "19899513-3be5-53f8-bf08-723fa2b9dad9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716916} {:answer/id #uuid "28684082-f7ca-586e-8166-e84c74a2e874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716919} {:answer/id #uuid "986d8caf-f85d-5cbd-a374-2ed99b92c868" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2-y^2=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716927} {:answer/id #uuid "9a55364f-5f6a-5d85-a550-a719e324df18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2=\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0786e72d-fdb6-5b51-a5bb-f94092553887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+y^2=\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716914} :answer-field/id #uuid "90ba2751-d6ff-5357-aa35-21c71fc6a4ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f68de867-63c2-5cb7-9bb4-c3b1ad94c187" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3}{2}\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\frac{3}{2}\\sin\\theta,\\quad 0\\leq\\theta<2\\pi.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Eliminate $\\theta$ using $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$.\n\nSquaring the $x$-equation and the $y$-equation gives\n\n$$\nx^2=\\frac{9}{4}\\cos^2\\theta,\\qquad y^2=\\frac{9}{4}\\sin^2\\theta.\n$$\n\nAdd the equations and factor out the common coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^2+y^2&=\\frac{9}{4}(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)\\\\\n&=\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot1\\\\\n&=\\frac{9}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is $x^2+y^2=\\frac{9}{4}$. Both numerator and denominator of the radius $\\frac{3}{2}$ are squared. The full parameter interval traces the entire circle."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32e312ef-38df-55d0-a292-8e586a713fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32e312ef-38df-55d0-a292-8e586a713fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716940} :answer-field/id #uuid "34876873-0a72-5506-82ba-acbbebe653ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "01ca9f59-062c-5d62-a4a1-5d091bddc512" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(C)$, given that\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n$\\det(C)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, multiply the main diagonal entries and subtract the product of the off-diagonal entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nEach diagonal contains two negative entries, so both products are positive. Keep the order: main-diagonal product minus off-diagonal product.\n\nThe determinant can be negative; determinant bars do not mean absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(C) &=(-2)(-5)-(-3)(-4) \\\\ &=10-12 \\\\ &=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03caa3a5-ae8d-5f2b-9f48-fb424e738839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716936} {:answer/id #uuid "05b10cba-f8c9-5089-a296-0732e8cb9e54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716937} {:answer/id #uuid "32f75a31-4b5c-5237-bde4-f27a2e1f5a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716941} {:answer/id #uuid "335df867-4021-5b0b-bb1e-478d114bed8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716942} {:answer/id #uuid "b40a3b19-da66-5ead-8bcf-931fec634843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32f75a31-4b5c-5237-bde4-f27a2e1f5a17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716941} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c23926e-5529-5d15-8af8-3d8b3e772218" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0aa10523-be4a-57fe-9858-f98da39469b6" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A)$, given that\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, multiply the main diagonal entries and subtract the product of the off-diagonal entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\n![The blue main diagonal gives ad; subtract bc from the red off-diagonal. ](images/25/2594f99e0f02241dc6d01f85c82923103df1d6fb4dda5ca03d438637f5178a28.png)\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(A) &=(2)(4)-(1)(3) \\\\ &=8-3 \\\\ &=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186716945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94466079-59c9-574e-a114-ce7e2fd929a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716946} {:answer/id #uuid "94e4532c-f041-5571-b77b-826e17dce420" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716947} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa7b27b-2a84-5cc3-840e-06bf1d8a9950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716949} {:answer/id #uuid "d9430131-9b2d-50d8-a884-36c769943088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716950} {:answer/id #uuid "ea5ea099-f7c9-573c-9426-c7b32f0c040e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea5ea099-f7c9-573c-9426-c7b32f0c040e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716951} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ccb7a7d-cec7-57f9-b016-76cbedd45391" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186716939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58f6ea98-a4e7-583f-b58c-838a38934da5" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(B)$, given that\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, multiply the main diagonal entries and subtract the product of the off-diagonal entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nThe off-diagonal product is negative: $(3)(-4)=-12$. Subtracting this negative product adds $12$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\det(B) &=(2)(1)-(3)(-4) \\\\ &=2-(-12) \\\\ &=2+12 \\\\ &=14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717046 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18304ae9-6066-5991-ad39-a6b24b05635e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-11\\sin\\theta,\\quad y=-11\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717043} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0c454d-1b7b-526f-9868-0a079576aecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11\\sin\\theta,\\quad y=11\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717053} {:answer/id #uuid "9e078946-c561-5e6f-8baf-babbb12ca01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-11\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=11\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717059} {:answer/id #uuid "cf62b8d2-7b92-545f-a1e6-ff6205072875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-11\\sin\\theta,\\quad y=11\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717064} {:answer/id #uuid "f2a18ae6-2c05-5246-8f4c-2521d81f4595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11\\sin\\theta,\\quad y=-11\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717070}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf62b8d2-7b92-545f-a1e6-ff6205072875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-11\\sin\\theta,\\quad y=11\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717064} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8f1df9a-3d34-5d62-93d2-f1a6d983f242" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717069}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19aafdc9-a556-56ea-839e-a2eda1c9f48c" :question/problem "![Circle centered at the origin, starting at A(0, 11), moving counterclockwise.](images/9f/9f3f09db56a7b67f79116f831677f9b1dc749a74d0631ca80dbd67d4b96d16a2.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $11$ centered at the origin, shown above. Which set of parametric equations will traverse the circle once counterclockwise, starting at $A(0,11)$ when $\\theta=0$? Use $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$ and one sine or cosine term with argument $\\theta$ in each equation." :question/worked-solution "The supplied radius is $11$, so each coordinate has amplitude $11$.\n\nAt $\\theta=0$, cosine is $1$ and sine is $0$. To start at $A(0,11)$, use sine in the $x$-coordinate and cosine in the $y$-coordinate. Choose the signs so that the next quarter-turn reaches $(-11,0)$, moving counterclockwise.\n\nThus the equations are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=-11\\sin\\theta\\\\\ny&=11\\cos\\theta.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $\\theta=0$ the point is $(0,11)$; at $\\theta=\\pi/2$ it is $(-11,0)$, confirming the start and direction. Both coordinate amplitudes are $11$, so the point remains on the required circle. As $\\theta$ runs through $[0,2\\pi)$, one full period traces the circle exactly once."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717054 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1712ed30-346e-5533-84e3-84ba3de2c909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-20\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=20\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717042} {:answer/id #uuid "1cf9720f-04d5-5cfc-8b86-92c7115d3a45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=20\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=-20\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717047} {:answer/id #uuid "2838cb44-af7c-57da-b78d-25cfd849b7dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=20\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=20\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717050} {:answer/id #uuid "2d79078e-0df5-5434-8641-8f3c6d0c8651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.