\\theta=0$ the point is $(0,20)$; at $\\theta=\\pi/2$ it is $(20,0)$, confirming the start and direction. Both coordinate amplitudes are $20$, so the point remains on the required circle. As $\\theta$ runs through $[0,2\\pi)$, one full period traces the circle exactly once."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717090 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbde0ea4-50ae-5e51-9ea1-5e8b2fd93514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbde0ea4-50ae-5e51-9ea1-5e8b2fd93514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717091} :answer-field/id #uuid "06b80108-f7d6-5852-8efd-a13a1030f18c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57b808a6-aa20-5184-984b-2b3aa60d1744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57b808a6-aa20-5184-984b-2b3aa60d1744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717085} :answer-field/id #uuid "113e12dd-64a1-5cae-9bee-44d6a3647d74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "baa213c0-d0ff-51c1-8e11-3b433d9e9955" :question/problem "![Circle centered at the origin, starting at A(-2, 0), moving counterclockwise.](images/b9/b909c3c1cbd9961d3c0d5c38fec91131d063c52b0674eea4a952911b59a97617.png)\n\nThe circle shown is centered at $O(0,0)$ and passes through the labeled point $A$. Construct a set of parametric equations that traverse the circle once counterclockwise, starting at $A$ when $\\theta=0$. Use $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$ and one sine or cosine term with argument $\\theta$ in each equation.\n\n$x=$ {{field-1}}, $y=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The axis point is $A(-2,0)$. Its distance from $O(0,0)$ is $2$, so the radius is $2$.\n\nAt $\\theta=0$, cosine is $1$ and sine is $0$. To start at $A(-2,0)$, use cosine in the $x$-coordinate and sine in the $y$-coordinate. Choose the signs so that the next quarter-turn reaches $(0,-2)$, moving counterclockwise.\n\nThus the equations are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=-2\\cos\\theta\\\\\ny&=-2\\sin\\theta.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $\\theta=0$ the point is $(-2,0)$; at $\\theta=\\pi/2$ it is $(0,-2)$, confirming the start and direction. Both coordinate amplitudes are $2$, so the point remains on the required circle. As $\\theta$ runs through $[0,2\\pi)$, one full period traces the circle exactly once."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717092 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "308bab30-f621-5c2d-bfe2-edd782456858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "308bab30-f621-5c2d-bfe2-edd782456858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\sin\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717083} :answer-field/id #uuid "26ba4c8f-f55d-5e4c-b703-ed7faca19f87" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ee83e6f-c230-543a-ab60-4ee001457ce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ee83e6f-c230-543a-ab60-4ee001457ce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20\\cos\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717087} :answer-field/id #uuid "76dd0f3d-e89d-566f-9a32-9b0b8a5999b6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dd69666c-b828-5283-a6cd-adfe4a8d7ff3" :question/problem "![Circle centered at the origin, starting at A(0, -20), moving counterclockwise.](images/7e/7e8459d554d63a52cdf1e506727d1d31ee8920454bdc32a9b5a79140a967c35c.png)\n\nThe circle shown is centered at $O(0,0)$ and passes through the labeled point $A$. Construct a set of parametric equations that traverse the circle once counterclockwise, starting at $A$ when $\\theta=0$. Use $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$ and one sine or cosine term with argument $\\theta$ in each equation.\n\n$x=$ {{field-1}}, $y=$ {{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "The axis point is $A(0,-20)$. Its distance from $O(0,0)$ is $20$, so the radius is $20$.\n\nAt $\\theta=0$, cosine is $1$ and sine is $0$. To start at $A(0,-20)$, use sine in the $x$-coordinate and cosine in the $y$-coordinate. Choose the signs so that the next quarter-turn reaches $(20,0)$, moving counterclockwise.\n\nThus the equations are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx&=20\\sin\\theta\\\\\ny&=-20\\cos\\theta.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $\\theta=0$ the point is $(0,-20)$; at $\\theta=\\pi/2$ it is $(20,0)$, confirming the start and direction. Both coordinate amplitudes are $20$, so the point remains on the required circle. As $\\theta$ runs through $[0,2\\pi)$, one full period traces the circle exactly once."}]}
